# ParlInfo Backfill Analysis

```elixir
alias ParliamentSearchAgent.Repo
alias ParliamentSearchAgent.Items.{Report, Broadcast, HearingTranscript}
import Ecto.Query
```

## Dataset Overview

Record counts and date coverage per dataset.

```elixir
datasets = [
  {"Reports", Report, :date_tabled},
  {"Hearing Transcripts", HearingTranscript, :date_tabled},
  {"Broadcasts", Broadcast, :start_time}
]

for {label, schema, date_field} <- datasets do
  {count, min_date, max_date} =
    Repo.one(
      from r in schema,
        select: {count(r.id), min(field(r, ^date_field)), max(field(r, ^date_field))}
    )

  IO.puts("#{label}: #{count} records | #{min_date} → #{max_date}")
end
```

## Year-by-Year Distribution — Reports

```elixir
from(r in Report,
  where: not is_nil(r.date_tabled),
  group_by: fragment("date_part('year', ?)", r.date_tabled),
  select: {fragment("date_part('year', ?)", r.date_tabled), count(r.id)},
  order_by: fragment("1")
)
|> Repo.all()
|> Enum.map(fn {year, count} -> %{year: trunc(year), count: count} end)
|> Kino.DataTable.new()
```

## Year-by-Year Distribution — Hearing Transcripts

```elixir
from(r in HearingTranscript,
  where: not is_nil(r.date_tabled),
  group_by: fragment("date_part('year', ?)", r.date_tabled),
  select: {fragment("date_part('year', ?)", r.date_tabled), count(r.id)},
  order_by: fragment("1")
)
|> Repo.all()
|> Enum.map(fn {year, count} -> %{year: trunc(year), count: count} end)
|> Kino.DataTable.new()
```

## Data Quality — Records Missing PDF URLs

Items that were backfilled without detail scraping.

```elixir
missing =
  from(r in Report,
    where: is_nil(r.pdf_url),
    select: %{title: r.title, date_tabled: r.date_tabled, parlinfo_id: r.parlinfo_id},
    order_by: [desc: r.date_tabled],
    limit: 200
  )
  |> Repo.all()

IO.puts("Reports missing PDF URL: #{length(missing)}")
Kino.DataTable.new(missing)
```

```elixir
missing_transcripts =
  from(r in HearingTranscript,
    where: is_nil(r.pdf_url),
    select: %{title: r.title, date_tabled: r.date_tabled, parlinfo_id: r.parlinfo_id},
    order_by: [desc: r.date_tabled],
    limit: 200
  )
  |> Repo.all()

IO.puts("Transcripts missing PDF URL: #{length(missing_transcripts)}")
Kino.DataTable.new(missing_transcripts)
```

## Recent Records

```elixir
from(r in Report,
  order_by: [desc: r.inserted_at],
  limit: 20,
  select: %{title: r.title, date_tabled: r.date_tabled, committee_name: r.committee_name}
)
|> Repo.all()
|> Kino.DataTable.new()
```

## Ad-hoc Exploration

```elixir
# Edit this cell freely — the full app context is available
from(r in Report,
  where: ilike(r.committee_name, "%Economics%"),
  order_by: [desc: r.date_tabled],
  limit: 20
)
|> Repo.all()
|> Kino.DataTable.new()
```
